  "about": "What `interceptor desktop` cannot do, or does only in part, on Windows and Linux. Every command not listed works on both. A row without `sub` covers the whole family (`except` names the subcommands that still work); `flag` narrows a row to one flag. scripts/gen-skills.ts writes these rows into each OS's interceptor-desktop skill, `interceptor desktop --help` and the MCP desktop menu hide the `no` rows, and test/desktop-support.test.ts checks every row against the parity cases it cites in scripts/desktop-parity/cases.",
